   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Mr. Would Please Help My Pony**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **I've Got To Put The Hammer Down**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **When The Going Gets Tough**: back after 412 archived shows (5700 days); rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2007-06-10** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 33 songs; 145 min [1]\n- **ween2007-06-10.remastered**: source not stated; 32 songs; 137 min [2]. Said about its sound: Remaster has clip restoration and parametric EQ, no hum or hiss; uploader rates quality top-grade, with crowd singing along loudly like a stadium [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2007-06-10**: taped by John Lynn; transferred by John Lynn; source: AKG Ck61 > A61 > JW Mod C460 > Apogee Mini-MP > Korg MR-1 All Hydra Audio Interconnects DIN at left side of board - WSD 2.8MHz @ 1bit [1]",
